From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:18:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: Seal of Flames randomizer: hear the New Game step

Round 82b (docs/ROUND82B_PLAN.md S1-S3; the owner's "Yes, that order" to
Grok's order in docs/collab/SEAL_EDITION_SPLIT_GROK.md). Round 82's new-parts
check N4 found that Seal of Flames + Normal + Classic with the randomizer on
gives the plain game, with no warning (the same answer on Casual is
randomized). The cause is round 81b's D1: it assumed the randomizer's hooks
are off on Seal, but this port's frontend keeps them on (F-047), so the 81b
gate (step_game: Fates only) kept Seal out of the New Game step.

- S1 (fates_rando_session.rs): step_game is true for Fates (None, "fates")
  and Seal of Flames ("seal"); any other name stays out (fail closed). The
  hooks decide: listens = hooks_on (the Fates title id and
  Config::fates_rando) && step_game. With the hooks on, Seal at the defaults
  now lays round 81's StartFromBeginning trap and hears the step, exactly as
  Fates has since round 81b; with Config::fates_rando false, no trap, no
  guest memory read and no warning, as in round 81.
- S2: the two warning lines ("This New Game did not use your seed." and
  "Classic New Games cannot start the randomizer in this setup; pick Casual
  or Phoenix.") apply on Seal too, the same words, once each.
- S3: nothing else changes: the randomizer's output (answer, run id, patch),
  round 81's rows and bytes, the Fates behaviour from round 81b, loads and
  the page. Doc comments that said the hooks are off for Seal (hooks_on,
  Config::fates_rando, fates_options module and svc_outcome) now say what
  the code does.

Tests: two assertions of round 81b changed on purpose, because they pinned
81b's wrong assumption: fates_rando_session
only_fates_itself_hears_the_new_game_step (renamed
fates_and_seal_hear_the_new_game_step_and_the_hooks_decide):
step_game(Some("seal")) and listens(TITLE, true, Some("seal")) were false,
now true; added: hooks off for Seal does not listen, no title does not
listen, an unknown or differently spelled name does not hear. fates_options
the_trap_is_wanted_for_the_rows_or_the_randomizer: "Seal with no row set: no
trap" becomes the trap with the hooks on, and no trap with the hooks off.
New: a_seal_classic_new_game_is_heard_at_the_trap_and_picks_once,
a_seal_casual_new_game_heard_and_watched_in_one_frame_is_one_pick,
seal_with_the_randomizer_hooks_off_lays_no_trap_at_the_defaults,
a_seal_refusal_or_a_trap_that_cannot_be_laid_is_said_once. Every other
round 81 / 81b test unchanged and passing (the Fates behaviour). Nine code
mutations each fail at least one test (build/r82b/code/planted.txt).
zakuro-core 275 passed in engine/target/zakuro-core-test, zakuro 131 passed
(2 ignored) in engine/target/zakuro-frontend-test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
